  "scope": "# Review: 3a4b67ab16ff layer-order public-emission repair\nTask/source: assignment `review-0aca3a8d8904ee79`; prototype `1da9ec2e9f911c60d0c4eef8fa723fddc4d9b401aabf0ee09d62dad01ab9aded` (baseline `6a10eeca53778c05de026e78bdb62ba225240df5d144d43767cebaa1ea33e1aa`).\nDefect: public bytes/IDs were safe, but physical writes followed private setting/seed order and a duplicate could be found after an earlier public write.\nRepair: precompute and validate the full batch, reject duplicate visible IDs before output creation, sort by `public_id`, then emit evidence.\nAuthority: production generator `c643621f6d5d606ea6b988bf7d67ec5486ef288c11dc7b0f3fe43a33a611cd31` and canonical rule `32c694357bd0` are unchanged.\nTests: two regressions were observed red before the fix; final focused layer-order suite is `20 passed`, and selected edit scope is `35 passed`.\nRacket evidence: two fixed-setting episodes, each with 3 demonstrations and 4 distinct queries; all labels/rivals pass and public IDs are physically emitted sorted.\nNVARC ticket: blind pair-4 prediction matched exactly; one fixed rule reproduced all 13 pairs (`ok`).\nTool ticket: the requested selected-authority sync is already implemented; the pinned task reports `already_synchronized`, so disposition is `implemented_close`.\nRemaining limit: the unchanged frozen production fixture cannot collect because this source-only packet lacks `puzzle_generators.per_puzzle.3a4b67ab16ff`.\nAssessment: routine task-local prototype repair; no production/variant approval or training admission is implied.\n",
